@startuml epm1-wire-layout
' ============================================================================
' PathMap report §5.2 — the EPM1 wire layout and where it embeds on each lane.
'
'   EPM1 ::= "EPM1" | version | mode | varint(|ACTree03|) | ACTree03
'            | varint(value_count) | value_count × (varint(|Par|) | protobuf(Par))
'
' Diagram type: a COMPONENT/RECTANGLE layout diagram, chosen because the fact
' being illustrated is BYTE ORDER AND CONTAINMENT — which segments appear, in
' which order, and inside which carrier field on each of the two lanes.  Flow
' arrows would misstate it; the wire is a static layout, not a process.
'
' Colour convention — one hue per concept:
'   TEAL   #B2DFDB/#00695C  the EPM1 magic/version/mode prefix
'   GREEN  #C8E6C9/#2E7D32  the ACTree03 topology arena (set AND map)
'   PURPLE #E1BEE7/#6A1B9A  the map-value table (map mode only)
'   BLUE   #BBDEFB/#1565C0  Lane P (prost / network-consensus) carrier
'   ORANGE #FFE0B2/#E65100  Lane B (bincode / cold-store) carrier
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4

title <b>EPM1 — one versioned trie snapshot, embedded verbatim on both lanes</b>\nset mode has NO value table; map values are enumerated in the arena's value order

rectangle "**The EPM1 snapshot** — one contiguous byte string, memoized `OnceLock<Vec<u8>>`, shared by the clone family" as EPM1 #FAFAFA {
  rectangle "`\"EPM1\"`\n4-byte magic" as Magic #B2DFDB
  rectangle "`version`\n= 1" as Version #B2DFDB
  rectangle "`mode`\nset | map" as Mode #B2DFDB
  rectangle "`varint(|ACTree03|)`\narena length" as ALen #C8E6C9
  rectangle "**ACTree03 arena**\nPathMap's compact-tree topology,\nverbatim from the accessor" as Arena #C8E6C9
  rectangle "`varint(value_count)`\n**map mode only**" as VCount #E1BEE7
  rectangle "`value_count ×`\n`(varint(|Par|) ‖ protobuf(Par))`\nvalues in **arena value order**,\nencoded by the **generated protobuf PDA**" as Values #E1BEE7
}

Magic -[hidden]right-> Version
Version -[hidden]right-> Mode
Mode -[hidden]right-> ALen
ALen -[hidden]right-> Arena
Arena -[hidden]right-> VCount
VCount -[hidden]right-> Values

rectangle "**Lane P — prost, network / consensus**\n`EPathMap` **field 9**, wiretype 2 (`bytes`)\ncopies the SAME snapshot byte string" as LaneP #BBDEFB
rectangle "**Lane B — bincode, cold store / LMDB**\nthe first `EPathMap` field\ncopies the SAME snapshot byte string" as LaneB #FFE0B2

EPM1 -[#1565C0,bold]-> LaneP : verbatim copy
EPM1 -[#E65100,bold]-> LaneB : verbatim copy

note bottom of LaneP #E3F2FD
  ★ **Neither surface reconstructs a `Vec<Par>`.**  A tag-9 `bytes`
  field costs prost **zero** message levels, and the generated
  decode PDA reads the snapshot without a recursion ceiling —
  depth 4,096 round-trips on a 256 KiB test stack.
end note

note bottom of LaneB #FFF8E1
  ★ **Set mode ends at the arena** — there is no value table to
  parse, and value-free terminating topology is representable
  (something a `ps: Vec<Par>` projection structurally cannot say).
end note

note right of Values #F3E5F5
  ★ The cold snapshot cost is linear in trie nodes plus encoded
  values.  A cached `EpmLayout` retains only the topology prefix,
  avoiding <latex>\Theta(d^2)</latex> retained suffix bytes in
  nested map-value chains.  Warm access is
  <latex>\mathcal{O}(1)</latex> before the caller's required copy.
end note

legend bottom
  |= cell |= meaning |
  |<#B2DFDB>| EPM1 prefix: magic · version · mode |
  |<#C8E6C9>| ACTree03 topology arena (both modes) |
  |<#E1BEE7>| map-value table (map mode only; generated-PDA encoded) |
  |<#BBDEFB>| Lane P carrier — prost field 9 |
  |<#FFE0B2>| Lane B carrier — bincode first field |
endlegend

@enduml
